  "notes": [
    "Why 4.9 um (detector D6): in D2 and D4 the core is saturated. Five Aug 2025 exposures put the star 3.3 to 3.8 arcsec east of Gaia while other frames of that visit sit about 1 arcsec west. Field stars match Gaia to 0.2 arcsec and a PSF fit gives the same shift; the cause, in the detector, is not identified. An earlier D4 build with two such frames gave 9.6 +/- 1.0 (Dec) and -2.7 +/- 1.8 (RA) arcsec/yr.",
    "Motion errors include the scatter between frames in each visit, not just the scatter about the fit.",
    "Detected means S/N of at least 5 in a 2 px aperture on the stacked image (noise from blank spots in the same stack) and a centre within 1.5 px of the prediction.",
    "Each frame saw a different wavelength, so brightness changes between visits mix real change with colour. Not a light curve.",
    "Only frames with no masked pixel in the aperture are averaged; 3 visits had none, so their values are lower limits.",
    "Scatter between frames is far above the pipeline's error estimate, so the error bars understate the real uncertainty.",
    "Brightness: light summed in a 3 px (18.5 arcsec) circle on each frame, minus the local sky, averaged per visit; no aperture correction."
  ],
